import json
def add_final_screen(d,P,new_page,para,table,picture,is_glasses):
 O=P/'engineering-v18-results';f=O/'final_available_data_screen.json'
 if not f.exists():return
 s=json.loads(f.read_text());new_page(d,'V18 Final material and clearance screens')
 para(d,'This is the final bounded screen on the current V18 geometry. It adds 500 material and load comparisons, 288 pivot clearance scenarios and 216 equivalent acceleration comparisons. These are calculated scenarios, not 1004 physical tests. All six saved CAD candidates were also measured for the hinge stack. No real part or Sony headphone was measured.')
 grades={r['grade']:r for r in s['material_cases'] if r['component']=='Band' and r['load_factor']==1};table(d,['Recorded material reference','Modulus MPa','Ideal load for the reference band movement N'],[[name,f"{r['reference_modulus_MPa']:.0f}",f"{r['force_for_same_reference2000_fixture_movement_N']:.2f}"] for name,r in grades.items()],[3.0,1.3,2.6])
 para(d,'The ten grade records come from the saved 14 October reference study. Their source links and date are retained in the CSV. We reused the latest band, tongue stop and fork results. At the same applied force, the ideal movement changes inversely with stiffness. At the same imposed movement, the force rises with stiffness. The table uses the movement produced by 2 N in the original 2000 MPa band fixture. It is not a measured force on a wearer.')
 para(d,'The scaling keeps Poisson ratio at 0.35 for every reference and assumes the same linear elastic geometry and supports. The PP value is a flexural proxy. The steel references concern wire data, not qualified formed strip. We did not change full assembly mass or simulate actual creep, fatigue, anisotropy, cover or foam behaviour. No material winner or manufacturing allowable is established.')
 positive=s['positive_pivot_fit_margin_cases'];para(d,'The nominal 4 mm bolt in a 4.3 mm pivot bore has 0.15 mm radial clearance. The screen varies diameter error, relative axis error and radial swelling or coating. '+str(positive)+' of 288 scenarios retain positive calculated clearance. This count is not a factory yield or reliability probability. The other scenarios show that chosen adverse error bounds can consume the nominal clearance; supplier capability remains unknown.')
 para(d,'All six saved CAD stacks show a nominal nut height of 3.2 mm and no bolt tip protrusion beyond the nut. Moving the nut outward as the reference disc spring relaxes gives about 3.01 mm overlap between the nominal solid envelopes. This is not a thread engagement or bolt strength pass. Real thread ends, shoulder length, locking, tolerances and calibrated spring position still need an assembly design and proof.')
 new_page(d,'V18 Retention result and end of screening')
 picture(d,'V18_final_retention_screen','Calculated demand under equivalent static acceleration and the proposed unmeasured hinge torque targets. This is not a drop or impact simulation.',5.9)
 para(d,'The earlier gravity check used one g. With the worst assumed moving mass and orientation, the proposed minimum torque of 64 Nmm is exhausted at about '+f"{s['minimum_calculated64Nmm_threshold_g']:.2f}"+' g of equivalent resultant acceleration. Some 1.5 g scenarios therefore exceed that target. The hinge permits inward folding by design. Static gravity holding does not establish resistance to accidental folding during carrying or movement.')
 para(d,'This is a risk found by a conditional calculation, not a measured failure of an assembled headphone. The calculation does not include a time history, inertia driven rotation, damping, friction changes or a retaining case. We need actual breakaway and running torque, ageing and handling measurements before choosing or changing the holding target. It would be misleading to call the headset durable or safely retained from these results.')
 table(d,['Current evidence','Decision'],[['Rigid CAD and saved poses','Recorded numerical checks completed'],['Band tongue and fork fixtures','Chosen component mesh comparisons completed under assumptions'],['Material clearance and retention screens','Completed finite scenarios with known limitations and retention risk'],['Complete joint contact and manufacturing','Still requires credible material contact and assembly inputs'],['Acoustics heat comfort and durability','Still requires physical measurements and assembled tests'],['Sony WH CH720N fit','Original pad and mount measurements are deferred']],[2.6,4.3])
 para(d,'The available data screening is now recorded. The product validation phase has not passed. The next useful step is to select and measure actual material samples and make a bench assembly, then calibrate the models against it. More arbitrary inputs would not measure sound reduction, leakage, comfort or material life. There is no manufacturing release or demonstrated advantage over market headphones.')
 if is_glasses:para(d,'The Sony replacement pad geometry is unchanged. These standalone hinge and material comparisons do not prove that the replacement fits the Sony, reduces glasses pressure or preserves bass, ANC, isolation or outgoing leakage.')
